   "text": "Mixing first. When chyme stretches the wall, the enteric nervous system triggers segmentation. Rings of circular muscle squeeze at spaced points, dividing the gut into a chain of sausages. Each set lasts a fraction of a minute. As it relaxes, a new set forms in between. Chyme barely moves forward. Instead, it's churned, blended with digestive juices, and pressed against the absorptive surface."
